clueweb09-en0008-71-01423.0 [Haunted Bay Logo] >> HOME > REVIEWS > Tunitas Creek Family Farm Thursday, 15-Jan-2009 04:12:58 PST [Search our articles.] [Search our calendar.] [] Tunitas Creek Family Farm Saturday, September 14th, marked our first Halloween field trip here at Haunted Bay. We took a leisurely drive to the Tunitas Creek Family Farm to pick up our first pumpkins of the season! It was good timing too as this was grand opening day. Arriving early in the season we had the rare pleasure of removing our pumpkins from the vines ourselves. Over the coming weeks the good people at Tunitas Creek Family Farm will be cutting the pumpkins off the vines for easy selection. Easy that is unless you are looking for that perfect pumpkin. There are plenty that will catch your eye making selecting difficult and the family assures us that in the next few weeks they will be bringing more
clueweb09-enwp01-83-02310.0 Pickard, Indiana From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia Jump to: navigation, search Pickard [Pickard is located in Indiana] [Pickard] Pickard Coordinates: 40ýý13ýýý23ýýýN 86ýý15ýýý41ýýýWýýý / ýýý40.22306ýýN 86.26139ýýWýýý / 40.22306; -86.26139 Country United States State Indiana County Clinton Township Sugar Creek Named for Jacob Pickard[1] Elevation [2] 928 ft (283 m) ZIP code 46050 FIPS code 18-59544[3] GNIS feature ID 441098 Pickard is an unincorporated town in Sugar Creek Township, Clinton County, Indiana. The town is named for Jacob Pickard who operated a sawmill at the site.[4] [edit] History Jacob Pickard ran a sawmill at Pickard's Mills. It was originally operated at Jefferson in the western part of the county, but James M. Ward, Jack Hill, and Frank McMannis moved it to the new site at a town then called Hillsborough. Jacob Pickard took over the mill and the town then came to be known as Pickard's Mill.[5] In 1851, the old mill
clueweb09-en0009-52-24958.0 [Falls Creek Farm] [] [Growers] Growers Best-quality vegetables and fruits make Falls Creek Farm the grower of choice for discerning consumers as well as restaurateurs, chefs and gourmands. Through our wholesaler, our renowned produce finds its way into some of the finest restaurants and hotels across New England. Our produce can also be purchased directly at our on-site garden retail store, which features baked goods, gourmet items and gifts. Be sure to stop in when visiting Falls Creek Farm during the growing season. Falls Creek Farm has been growing fine produce for family and friends since 1987. In 1995, we expanded our operation and began to grow commercially. Since that time, Falls Creek Farm has earned a reputation as the regions premier grower of high-end produce. We attribute our success to our team of dedicated and experienced growers, who have spent decades honing their craft. Led by Falls Creek Farm
