clueweb09-en0010-87-24883.0 Show Results [2008 Western Championship] Click on the picture to read our Foaling Chronicles Miniature horses are the smallest breed in the equine world. Scott Creek Miniature Horse Farm is one of the few and leading breeders of Arabian style miniature horses. With over twenty-five years experience in miniature horse breeding, our farm has selectively bred the finest AMHA registered horses. Our horses exhibit the ultimate in elegance, refinement, proportion, and exquisite movement. Scott Creek Miniature Horse Farm is world recognized as a miniature horse breeder of exceptional miniature horses for show in both the halter and performance arena. Breeding farms consistently look to Scott Creek Miniature Horses as a source for upgrading their breeding programs. Our site is provided to everyone who is interested in learning more about ”minis". The site includes technical information to owners about horse health and management. You can also learn about our farm, the
clueweb09-en0011-52-03396.0 [Hosted by USGenNet] CLAY COUNTY CEMETERIES Taken from Clay, Jackson, and Putnam Counties, Tennessee, an index by Charles A. Reeves, Jr. Those marked with an asterisk (*) are identified on the Clay County map. Most of these entries are from Walter Webb's book (Clay County, Tennessee Tombstone Inscriptions; Walter E. Webb; Dale Hollow Lake; Celina, TN 38551; used with permission). Those with old dates in brackets are from earlier references and may have been renamed and/or may be duplicates of other entries. A few cemeteries are shown on the USGS topo maps that aren't listed elsewhere; these have numbers above 267 and are listed twice to aid in location, by both number and alphabetical. No. Name Location Map Grid No. 1 *Varney Andrews Cemetery Near the West end of the Cumberland River Bridge on the West bank of Highway 52 between the Kyle house and Proctor Creek. D2(?) 2 *Evan
